  "rounds": {
    "1": {
      "note": "Modal verbs go right before the main verb to express wanting, ability, or permission. 想 (soeng2) = want to · 要 (jiu3) = need to / must · 可以 (ho2 ji5) = can / may · 會 (wui5) = will / be able to · 識 (sik1) = know how to (a skill) · 鍾意 (zung1 ji3) = like to. Negate with 唔 (m4): 唔想 (m4 soeng2, don’t want to), 唔可以 (m4 ho2 ji5, may not), 唔識 (m4 sik1, don’t know how).",
